      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine how long it takes for the squirrel to travel 1 mile at a constant speed of 4 miles per hour. Here are the steps:\n\n1. **Understand the given information:**\n   - Speed of the squirrel: 4 miles per hour\n   - Distance to be traveled: 1 mile\n\n2. **Use the formula for time:**\n   The formula to calculate time when speed and distance are known is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Speed}}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Substitute the known values into the formula:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Time} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{4 \\text{ miles per hour}}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Perform the division:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Time} = \\frac{1}{4} \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Convert the time from hours to minutes:**\n   Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, we multiply the time in hours by 60:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Time in minutes} = \\left(\\frac{1}{4} \\text{ hours}\\right) \\times 60 \\text{ minutes per hour}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Calculate the result:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Time in minutes} = \\frac{60}{4} = 15 \\text{ minutes}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, it takes the squirrel \\boxed{15} minutes to travel 1 mile.",
